      "baseline": "pre-update-installed-claude",
      "path": "feature-forge/scripts/build_feature_docs.py",
      "sha256": "6d45a3b90f6b60925f17b0e53ba2a47ef0bbcdfd5d3dd719df52f2301ade3fff",
      "headings": [
        "# The cross-build document fixes and the style loader have ONE source, in the",
        "# sibling shared-assets skill folder. The header carries a <!-- SHARED_ASSETS -->",
        "# and a <!-- STCLAIR_DOC_STYLE --> placeholder; resolve_header() returns a",
        "# temporary header with both filled in.",
        "# (filename prefix, nav label). Order is the nav order.",
        "# Set by main(): which SPECS prefixes exist in this folder (so the nav never",
        "# links a doc the feature does not have), and the",
        "# crucible's built file name (00_crucible.md or 00_crucible_<feature>.md).",
        "# Set by main(): the style CSS read once per build, and whether to number",
        "# sections (the default; --plain turns it off).",
        "# The pandoc template. It gives the page nothing of pandoc's own default",
        "# styles; the build assembles <main> from the three marked pieces.",
        "# (insight classes, label). None means no tint: the label and the content",
        "# only, as quiet labelled prose. A requirement is a spec fact, not a point to",
        "# carry forward, so it does not get a panel.",
        "# Verdict word -> the style's status-dot colour.",
        "# Finding identifiers used in disposition tables and review prose (RF1, S2, C1,",
        "# Q3, K1, ...). The `#` column of a disposition table links down to the matching",
        "# verbatim entry in the merged reviews so the human can jump spec \u2192 detail.",
        "# Block containers an <h2> can sit inside. Only an <h2> outside all of them",
        "# opens a section; one inside a callout, a list item or a quote stays put.",
        "# An authored links row. The source carries one so the page served live by",
        "# `lahe review` has it; the build draws its own, linked to the built pages.",
        "# A link to a sibling spec doc by its Markdown name. The source links .md so",
        "# the live page works; the built dossier links the built page instead."
      ]
    },
